cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Colour palettes for medium and deep skin tones (Monk 3-9)
message: If you use this dataset, please cite it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Pareek
    given-names: Shashank
    affiliation: Varna Code
    city: Jaipur
    country: IN
repository-code: "https://github.com/thevarnacode/skin-tone-colour-palettes"
url: "https://varnacode.in"
abstract: >-
  Eight skin tones spanning Monk 3-9 and twenty-four colour palettes (192
  colours with hex values), anchored to the Monk Skin Tone Scale, with
  undertone treated as an axis separate from depth. Includes season-assigned
  neutrals and a four-term taxonomy for classifying two-colour combinations.
  Built for medium and deep skin, which the Western seasonal and Korean
  personal-colour systems were not designed around.
keywords:
  - colour analysis
  - color analysis
  - skin tone
  - Monk Skin Tone Scale
  - melanin rich skin
  - deep skin tones
  - South Asian
  - personal color
  - colour palette
